pam-rssh (1.2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reject security-key signatures whose FIDO user-presence flag is clear
    (sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com, sk-ecdsa-sha2-nistp256@openssh.com), matching
    sshd. Keys created with -O no-touch-required now fail unless their
    authorized_keys entry allows them. (#38, #39)
  * Add the no-touch-required option to authorized_keys entries and to the
    output of authorized_keys_command. (#38, #39)
  * Add the challenge=<random|pam_ssh_agent_auth> module option. With
    challenge=pam_ssh_agent_auth the ssh-agent signs the request details
    (users, PAM service, command line, working directory, host name, time and
    a random cookie) in pam_ssh_agent_auth's format, so an agent that confirms
    signatures can show which command is being approved. (#40)
  * Read the command line from the process arguments and the host name with
    gethostname(), so the request also works on macOS, which has no /proc.
  * Log to LOG_USER on macOS, where libsyslog has no LOG_AUTH. (#41)
  * Build RPMs for Fedora 45 (x86_64 and aarch64). (#42)
  * Document the authorized_keys options and the challenge option.

 -- Yuxiang Zhang <z4yx@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

pam-rssh (1.2.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace syslog crate with libsyslog (native system syslog)
  * Add RPM packages for more distributions (Fedora, RHEL-compatible Rocky Linux)

